  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\nIssued at 111 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nPost frontal low clouds cover a large part of the middle\nMississippi and Ohio River Valleys early this afternoon. The\ncloud deck has pushed to near the TN/MS line. The latest RAP\nindicates that the deck will gradually push south into north MS\nand then gradually clear out later tonight from the northeast.\nHigh pressure over the Upper Mississippi Valley will build across\nthe Mid-South this weekend leading to cool and dry conditions.\nClearing skies and diminishing winds will result in temps\ndropping into the 30s across northern parts of the Mid-South\nlater tonight. The latest NBM shows a chance (30-40%) of freezing\ntemps across parts of West Tennessee Saturday morning.\n\nA 1024 mb surface high be centered over the region by Saturday\nnight with chilly temps. Highs on Saturday will only reach the\nupper 50s to lower 60s with plenty of sunshine. Excellent\nradiational cooling conditions Sunday morning will likely result\nin a freeze across portions of northeast Arkansas, the Missouri\nBootheel, West Tennessee and north Mississippi.\n\nThe weather pattern remains fairly benign through the week. High\npressure will remain over the area into the middle of the week\nand temperatures will gradually moderate with highs warming\ntoward 70 degrees and lows in the 40s. A weak upper level\ndisturbance moving through during the Tuesday/Tuesday night\ntimeframe could bring a shower. A deep trough developing over the\neastern CONUS toward Thursday will send a cold front and perhaps\na few showers through the Mid-South before ushering in cooler\ntemperatures and mostly dry weather to close out the week.",
